# GUIShop Special Item Configurations

This covers non-standard item types that require special configuration.

## Spawners

```yaml
'10':
  type: SHOP
  id: SPAWNER
  buy-price: 5000
  mob-type: ZOMBIE  # EntityType name
```

- Uses Bukkit's `CreatureSpawner` API
- `mob-type` sets the spawned entity

## Potions

```yaml
'11':
  type: SHOP
  id: POTION  # or SPLASH_POTION, LINGERING_POTION
  buy-price: 100
  potion-info:
    type: SPEED  # PotionType name
    splash: false
    extended: true   # Duration extended
    upgraded: false  # Level II
```

- Parsed in `Item.java` → `PotionInfo` object
- Applied via `PotionMeta.setBasePotionType()`

## Tipped Arrows

```yaml
'12':
  type: SHOP
  id: TIPPED_ARROW
  buy-price: 20
  potion-info:
    type: HARMING
    splash: false
    extended: false
    upgraded: true
```

## Fireworks

```yaml
'13':
  type: SHOP
  id: FIREWORK_ROCKET
  buy-price: 50
  firework-info:
    flight: 2  # Flight duration (1-3)
    explosions:
      - type: BALL_LARGE  # BALL, BALL_LARGE, STAR, BURST, CREEPER
        colors: "255,0,0 0,255,0"  # RGB values space-separated
        fade-colors: "255,255,255"
        flicker: true
        trail: true
```

- Multiple explosions supported
- Colors are RGB triplets

## Enchantments

```yaml
'14':
  type: SHOP
  id: DIAMOND_SWORD
  buy-price: 500
  enchantments: "SHARPNESS:5 UNBREAKING:3 FIRE_ASPECT:2"
```

- Space-separated `ENCHANT:LEVEL` pairs
- Uses Bukkit enchantment names

## Player Heads (Skulls)

```yaml
'15':
  type: SHOP
  id: PLAYER_HEAD
  buy-price: 100
  skull-uuid: "b1e4c2a7-..."  # Player UUID
  # OR use base64 texture:
  skull-uuid: "eyJ0ZXh0dXJlcyI6eyJTS0lOIjp7InVybCI6..."
```

- `SkullCreator.java` handles texture application

## Command Items

```yaml
'16':
  type: COMMAND
  id: NETHER_STAR
  buy-price: 1000
  shop-name: "&6&lSpecial Reward"
  sudo: false  # false=console (default), true=run as player
  commands:
    - "give {PLAYER_NAME} diamond 64"
    - "broadcast {PLAYER_NAME} bought the special reward!"
```

**Command Placeholders:**
- `{PLAYER_NAME}` - Player's username
- `{PLAYER_UUID}` - Player's UUID
- `{PLAYER_WORLD}` - Player's current world name
- `{PLAYER_BALANCE}` - Player's economy balance

**Sudo Mode:**
- `sudo: false` (default) - Commands run as CONSOLE
- `sudo: true` - Commands run as the player (useful for permission-based commands)

- Item is NOT given to player (only commands run)

## Shop Shortcuts (Menu Navigation)

```yaml
'17':
  type: SHOP_SHORTCUT  # In menu.yml typically
  id: DIAMOND
  name: "&bGems Shop"
  target-shop: Gems  # Shop name to open
  lore:
    - "&7Click to browse gems"
```

- Opens another shop when clicked
- Used in menu.yml for shop buttons

## Custom Model Data

```yaml
'18':
  type: SHOP
  id: PAPER
  buy-price: 10
  custom-model-data: 12345  # For resource pack models
```

## Item Flags

```yaml
'19':
  type: SHOP
  id: DIAMOND_SWORD
  buy-price: 200
  enchantments: "SHARPNESS:1"
  item-flags: "HIDE_ENCHANTS HIDE_ATTRIBUTES"
```

- Space-separated Bukkit ItemFlag names

## Navigation Items

These are used in shop/menu configs for GUI navigation:

```yaml
# Pagination - usually in bottom row (slots 45-53)
'48':
  type: PAGE_LEFT
  id: ARROW
  name: "&ePrevious Page"

'49':
  type: PAGE_STATUS
  id: NETHER_STAR
  name: "&7Page {CURRENT_PAGE} of {TOTAL_PAGES}"

'50':
  type: PAGE_RIGHT
  id: ARROW
  name: "&eNext Page"

# Player balance display
'45':
  type: PLAYER_BALANCE
  id: GOLD_INGOT
  name: "&6Balance: {PLAYER_BALANCE}"

# Back button (returns to menu from shop)
'53':
  type: BACK
  id: RED_STAINED_GLASS_PANE
  name: "&cBack"
```

**Notes:**
- Navigation items don't show buy/sell lore (not purchasable)
- `PAGE_LEFT`/`PAGE_RIGHT` auto-hide when on first/last page
- `{CURRENT_PAGE}`, `{TOTAL_PAGES}`, `{PLAYER_BALANCE}` are replaced dynamically
- `rows: N` config (1-6) determines available slots per page
